          "body": "Control Tower and Shift Brief consume one authenticated atomic operator snapshot. Navigation preserves selected subjects and ordinary refreshes; stale and unavailable data remain visible.\n\nOperators can inspect and revoke durable sessions. Lost revocation acknowledgements retain credentials, with explicit local-forget recovery. Generated models validate responses, and component launchers provision bootstrap files privately.\n\nValidation on f946cdc648c4ca5225a7b60eb9cbe12b31425343: complete local required passed, including 214 unit tests, 14 mocked browser tests, typed build, lint, security and docs. All six required jobs passed in both current GitHub runs (34430006326 and 34430000472). Source packets received independent static review; test inventories use observed identities.\n\nMatching Kernel changes are merged in neverhuman/bullet-kernel#4. These component results do not establish connected installation, provider execution, native controls, independent integration or authenticated showcase recordings. Operating HOLD remains effective.\n",
